Fix build with llvm-23

LLVM 24 moved the per-ISA SGPR/VGPR geometry, feature bitsets and LDS/wave
sizes into TargetParser tables.  LLVM 23 does not expose them, so bridge
what COMGR queries in comgr-metadata.cpp:

 - SGPR helpers rebuilt from the LLVM 23 ISA version rules.
 - getFeatureBitset() and the numeric getters backed by a static snapshot
   of the LLVM 24 tables, generated from the therock-10.2 llvm fork by
   replicating -gen-amdgpu-target-def semantics (see the provenance
   comment above the table).  A GPU that LLVM 23 can name but the table
   cannot describe is reported as an invalid ISA instead of yielding
   zeroed metadata.

Derived from the 10.1.0 compat patch; its comgr-isa-metadata.def and
include hunks are obsolete (file removed, gfx1250-strict gone upstream).
